    "title": "State Updates Ballast Water Rules to Protect Local Freshwater and Brackish Areas - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 hours ago The California State Lands Commission plans to readopt emergency changes to Article 4.7 of Chapter 1, Division 3, Title 2 of the California Code of Regulations. The rules apply to vessels with ballast water salinity below 18 parts per thousand.\nThe proposed regulations require these vessels to exchange ballast water before discharging in California’s fresh and brackish waters. This action adds to the state’s current ballast water discharge standards to help prevent invasive species and pollution.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.\n1",
